From fafdba3c2320b6208827a2c5713995f3a923517f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Sam (local build)" <sam@local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:52:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] dde_emu v1d: 0x5C NM (KL15/NM-gated, 60 s hard
 ceiling), 0x10A/0x142/0x68, KL15 from 0xF1, FIFO top-up, stats v4

- 0x5C: allowed while KL15 on, 47 s (9400 cycles) after KL15 off, or 1.76 s (352 cycles)
  after wake when KL15 was not on; never 60 s after max(wake, last KL15-on evidence)
- KL15: 0xF1 payload[2] 0x20 on / 0xE0 off (5 s timeout) once seen in a wake, else 0x103
  within 500 ms; core 0 hands 0xF1 to core 1 (dde_emu_on_frame, mailbox)
- 0x142 L31 (CTR8 B0 0..254, every 4 cycles, 3 content phases), 0x10A L5 00 ff ff ff
  (KL15 only, +39 cycles), 0x68 L3 c0 ff (every 1000 cycles); E8 L5 start 45 cycles
- minislot use from the frame length formula (table), MS limit 275
- frames > 8 words: preload 8, top up after the fire (50 us guard -> FAULT 1)
- dynamic alarm lead 10 us, housekeeping kept 200 us away from a slot alarm
- stats v4 (256 bytes, v3 layout unchanged up to 192): v1d counters, KL15/NM state,
  ISR latency min/max, top-up timeouts, abs cycle
- build switches EMU_DYN_5C / EMU_142 / EMU_10A / EMU_68 / EMU_KL15_F1 (all 1)
